  "comments": "Different mintmarks (castle = (HM), Hamburg Mint, crowned &quot;b&quot; = Bizuterie Jablonec Czech Mint)<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/56daa4b903e8e.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/56daa4b903e8e.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nTwo main groups of Reverse dies are known.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Reverse</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span> - shallow outline of script, the lower line of ribbon behind the horse was forgotten to draw.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span> - deep outline of script, the lower line of ribbon behind the horse is shown clearly.<br /><br />\r\nThe dies have many other feathers, by which they differ, these a just the two which are enough for attribution.<br /><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-style:italic;\">Combinations</span><br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">A</span>: 1993-1994.<br />\r\nDie <span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">B</span>: 1995- .<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/6118df001e0f0.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/6118df001e0f0.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"160\" /></a>",
